   "text": "This is my reading of the drawing, written as a linear peptide with the disulfide closed by a ring-closure label. Stereocentres are set from the drawing for L-Cpa and from the name for the rest.\n\n**Sequence (N to C):** Cpa \u2013 D-Cys \u2013 Tyr \u2013 D-Phe(4-phenylureido) \u2013 Lys \u2013 Thr \u2013 Cys \u2013 D-Tyr-NH2. The two Cys residues are joined by a disulfide bond.\n\n**Residue by residue:**\n- **Cpa:** 4-chlorophenylalanine at the free N-terminus. From the hashed NH2 in the drawing I get the S (L) configuration.\n- **D-Cys (position 2):** its sulfur is the one that closes the S\u2013S ring.\n- **Tyr:** L, with a free phenol.\n- **D-Phe(4-phenylureido):** the para position of the ring carries NH\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013phenyl.\n- **Lys:** L, with a free side-chain NH2.\n- **Thr:** L, so a (2S,3R) pattern with a free OH. I derived its SMILES from the standard L-Thr string.\n- **Cys:** L, the second sulfur of the disulfide.\n- **D-Tyr-NH2:** the C-terminal primary amide.\n\nI took the D/L assignments for all residues except Cpa from the name rather than re-deriving each from the wedges.\n\nSMILES: N[C@@H](Cc1ccc(Cl)cc1)C(=O)N[C@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@@H](Cc2ccc(O)cc2)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc3ccc(NC(=O)Nc4ccccc4)cc3)C(=O)N[C@@H](CCCCN)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N[C@@H](CS%10)C(=O)N[C@H](Cc5ccc(O)cc5)C(N)=O"
